In ftp://ftp.mcs.vuw.ac.nz/pub/statistics/map there are some
files with .l and .g extensions.  These are S-Plus for Windows versions
of the database files.  In particular, there are databases for
world.full, world.thin, world2 (Pacific-centric) and world2.thin.

I suggest you try a thinned version first, to get the mechanism sorted
out before you download the larger files.

You need 3 files, .g, .l, and .N the latter being a pure text file
common to all architectures (except perhaps for the end-of-line
character).  You need to find where to put these files to make them
accessible to the maps library.  I don't have a Windows system, so I
can't be any more specific than that, sorry.

Have fun!
