> The reason is in Splus 6 the condition (tmp2<=2) gives logical(0)
> whereas SPlus2000 gives NA.

Yes, the recycling rules are different. tmp2<=2 is now logical(0), not NA,
and so !is.element(tmp1,dp)|tmp2<=2 is also logical(0).

> Is there any function in Splus6 which can modify such code automatically
> ?

You just need to write it correctly ... I suspect you meant || not |.

