From: dsmith at insightful.com (David Smith)
Date: Thu, 29 Nov 2001 08:48:01 -0800
Subject: Re: Allowable names for sapply arguments
In-Reply-To: <Pine.GSO.4.10.10111291031160.28119-100000@phz-6>
References: <Pine.GSO.4.10.10111291031160.28119-100000@phz-6>
Message-ID: <LFEOLJDPHEIPIBEOGDDBKEDEEBAA.dsmith@insightful.com>

> Oh! So it is no good to use 'X' as an auxilliary argument to sapply?

Nope -- in fact, X is the first argument of sapply, as listed in
help(sapply) and in:

> args(sapply)
function(X, FUN, ..., simplify = T)

By passing X as a named argument, you are actually calling:

sapply(X=1, FUN=1:3, function(x,X) {print(x)})

hence the error.  The same applies to lapply.

# David

